node_modules/
dist/
# The e2e build: dist/ with a manifest that declares the content script statically, because a
# host grant cannot be performed from automation. e2e/harness.ts argues it.
dist-test/

# Release packages belong to a GitHub Release, not to the history — `npm run package` rebuilds
# any of them from the tag it was cut at.
piko-*.zip

# Output of npm run icons:sheet — something to look at once, not an artifact to keep.
icon-sheet.png

# Local agent scratch: worktrees are checkouts of this same repo, never content.
.claude/worktrees/

# What a failing browser test leaves behind, in both the places Vitest writes it. Kept on disk,
# because a picture of the frame is the fastest way to read a geometry failure — and out of the
# history, because every one of them was committed by accident and every one of them documents a
# bug that was fixed in the same session. Nothing here is a baseline: no test calls
# toMatchScreenshot, so nothing compares against these. Un-ignore the directory the day one does.
.vitest-attachments/
__screenshots__/
